# Original Commodore 64 Bruce Lee

Aim to be truthful to the original *Bruce Lee* on the Commodore 64. Movement, timing, poses, collision, graphics, and room data should follow that game.

When a behavior is unclear, check the assembly in `referencematerial\Bruce Lee.d64` before deciding. It is a Commodore 64 floppy disk image of the original game. Do not guess a mechanic, timing, or layout that the disk image can settle.

The VICE Commodore 64 emulator is on the system path. Run the floppy disk image with `x64sc "referencematerial\Bruce Lee.d64"`, or load a snapshot of the first scene with `x64sc "referencematerial\emulatorsnapshots\room00.vsf"`. The other room snapshots are in that same folder. Use that to verify the game against the original.

A 6502 disassembly of the code in memory, taken from that snapshot, is in `referencematerial\asm\game.asm`. The room tables are in `referencematerial\asm\rooms.asm`. Read those before disassembling the snapshot again.
